{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1189784-help-please-in-putting-my-character-to-paper","id":1189784,"title":"Help please in putting my character to paper","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-26T22:34:25-08:00","id":1189784,"title":"Help please in putting my character to paper","content":"It's no secret that I love Warhammer 40k. It's also no secret that I love changeling (and exalted). So why am I here...well allow me to introduce you to my Ogre Razorhand<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/KWIpkrDmpx4?t=19s\" data-code=\"KWIpkrDmpx4\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/KWIpkrDmpx4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> Yet he's inspired heavily on Abbadon the Despoiler. This was at first a panicked choice of picture because everyone had already picked what they looked like and I panicked and grabbed this image.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/417594640825581573/417900895498534912/unknown.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> So now I'm trying to figure out how to make him as a Ogre razor hand in Changeling 2e.<br /> Here is the story I have so far. My keeper was fascinated by the narrative of these weird games mortals play. So she found the perfect mortal. Someone who she thought could help change the narrative of one game for one faction. Then she grabbed a few others to oppose me, gave us armies of hobs...and I failed. So outraged was she that I failed at her experiment, when she thought I should have won, that she made new armor for me made from spite, anger, and wrath. Then he lined the insides with flesh hooks and super heated all but one piece and welded it to my remade body. The armor was designed to help me win, that combined with the special sword and projectile weapon she grafted into my body.<br /> <br /> The second time around I won because I had help a strategy posed by a friend of mine, and fellow slave of our master and I used my wrath and power to break apart the fake little demi-world I was waging my crusade in. In that moment...a loyalist (to our keeper) playing the part of an angelic saint cut me open and nearly gave me a spine-ectomy. that moment though... as that world crumbled around us, that was all we needed to escape into the hedge.<br /> <br /> So...here is the question...I have 10 merit points...and 3 tokens that I can see.<br /> 1- Sentient Sword that has a chance to harm me instead of attacking.<br /> 2- Black armor (high quality)<br /> 3 - A fey crafted automatic weapon that fires from two barrels at once...<br /> <br /> I would like to get this done with 2 merit points left for anything else like resources, but if all 10 are taken up in what I stole from that manipulative fey witch I'll take it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 02-27-2018, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T05:17:52-08:00","id":1189835,"title":"","content":"are you sure you want to use up all your starting Merit dots on Tokens instead of fighting styles, Giant and other things that could make you more formidable with any weapon? Perhaps just model your armor as part of your attributes and merits if its stuck to your body and have a plot-line going where you search for your old weapons that you lost in the Hedge?<br /> <br /> Also, why razorhand? Just asking","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 02-27-2018, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T05:37:56-08:00","id":1189840,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7920_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7920\" data-vbnamecard=\"7920\">Master Aquatosic</a> Good question, The short answer is...because I blurted out Ogre Razor hand first. Found the picture second because in a panic a space marine with a talon like lightning claw was exactly what I thought of when I thought Big strong guy with a Razor hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T05:38:43-08:00","id":1189841,"title":"","content":"So I know I mentioned the tokens a lot but I was sleepy and those were foremost on my mind. The other thing I should have mentioned with Kith. Luckily I found this. wonderful write up on the Kith update thread by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11755-aquatica1000\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11755_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11755\" data-vbnamecard=\"11755\">Aquatica1000</a>,<br /> <b>Razorhand</b><br /> <i>The Fae wanted me to be a mindless weapon, to kill whatever they want. Well, no more. This blade is mine, and I'll choose whose blood to spill.</i><br /> When the Fae make a Razorhand, they\u2019re looking for someone who can kill with ease, whether as an assassin striking from the shadows or a bodyguard cutting down those who stand in their master\u2019s way. To that end, the Razorhands are taken by forced and altered \u2013 oftentimes via the painful implementation of some type of blade into their hands and fingers \u2013 only to then be used as living weapons. It is often with these skills that the changelings often slip their captors.<br /> Once away from Arcadia, though, the Razorhands still must figure out what to do with their newfound freedom. There are plenty who turn to the summer court, eager to turn their combat skill to good use, but there are others still who use their skills to strike fear. And then there are those who, remorseful for those they have slain, turn to pacifism to atone for their sins.<br /> <i>Beast:</i> He\u2019s got the slitted eyes and striped pelt of a tiger, as well as the cocky attitude befitting one. When the going gets tough, though, he\u2019s quick to demonstrate to his foes that his claws aren\u2019t just meant to look pretty.<br /> <i>Elemental: </i>She is a representation of metal as a means of violence, with wiry hair and an expression one aggravation away from staring daggers. Sharp blades extend out of her hands almost naturally, as if she were born from them.<br /> <b>Blessing: </b>When a Razorhand charges at a target and makes an unarmed attack, three successes on the Brawl roll counts as an exceptional success.<br /> <i>Aim to Maim:</i> The Razorhand can choose to inflict lethal damage with his unarmed weapon (if the Changeling can already inflict lethal damage with unarmed attacks via abilities such as the Beast Seeming, it adds to the base damage by 1). In addition, by spending a point of Glamour and rolling Strength + Weaponry, the Razorhand can choose to automatically inflict one of the following Tilts in the next successful unarmed attack: Arm Wrack, Blinded, Deafened, or Leg Wrack.<br /> <br /> \u200bAwesome. Okay one step down, still thinking about the tokens I think I have an idea for that ranged weapon...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u><b>Pacifier of Violent Dreams</b></u></span></span><br /> Grafted into the flesh of a razor handed servant this weapon turns glamour into solid slugs of deep biting, explosive deadly malice. While it rests this fae crafted weapon rests upon it's symbiotic partners hand and is virtually weightless it's mask causing it to appear as a spiked glove upon it's owners hand. Once fed ammunition it wakes up and becomes visible to those who view it, seeing to cast aside it's mask. In reality the weapon retreats into the hand of it's owner so that only a bulge and a spinned ridge is seen on the back of the hand while it rests. The weapon awakens and readies for battle it rises up out of the body of it's owner.<br /> <b>Blessing:</b> The weapon is functionally two heavy SMG working together with armor piecing high explosive rounds as ammunition. It has the following stat line..<br /> Hurt Locker Variant: Damage 3, Range Medium, Capacity High, Iniative -3, Min Strength 3 Size 2, 9 Again AP1<br /> Core Variant: Damage 3, Range 50/100/200 Clip 30+1, Initiative -3, Min strength 3, Size 2, Burst fire 9 again Armor Piercing 1<br /> <b>Catch:</b> If the host spends 1 round protecting an individual they have perviously no known connection, and takes at least 1L damage from doing so, with from violence then the weapon may be activated and fed for free.<br /> <b>Drawback: </b>Any time the host rolls an attack, and at least 1 one appears in the roll they must roll all the 1's that appeared. Successes cause 1B damage to the host as the weapons recoil harms them. If the number of 1's rolled in the attack exceeds the host's stamina they take an arm wrack tilt in addition to any damage from those dice.<br /> Special: Surgicaly implanted - just possessing this token causes the host 1L damage that cannot be healed as long as they have the implant. If the implant is removed for any reasons other than the loss of the arm it deal 2L additional to the host.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking that's a Level 2 token?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":".  Giving ammo restriction 02-27-2018, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T06:04:47-08:00","id":1189846,"title":"","content":"that is 4 dots at least, even with the drawback. having a hidden smg with potentially infinite ammo if you feed off your enemies' Fear and Wrath is something you shouldn't be getting till mid-game at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T06:14:26-08:00","id":1189848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1189784-help-please-in-putting-my-character-to-paper?p=1189846#post1189846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that is 4 dots at least, even with the drawback. having a hidden smg with potentially infinite ammo if you feed off your enemies' Fear and Wrath is something you shouldn't be getting till mid-game at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait...so my token, that is causing me 1 persistent lethal damage that cannot be healed. that risks hurting me, cannot effectively do the same thing that a mere human can do with a holster and a long coat which they can get for free?<br /> <br /> But I agree with you on the ammo thing and set it to 30+1 which is the standard load for the weapon I used as the baseline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 02-27-2018, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T10:00:29-08:00","id":1189910,"title":"","content":"Oh. Didnt see that other drawback. Still thinking three dots","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T12:00:10-08:00","id":1189961,"title":"","content":"Okay.<br /> Other than the fact it can be concealed, like the mundane version of the weapon, what pushes it up that high? So I can get my mind around scope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T12:15:59-08:00","id":1189972,"title":"","content":"Doesnt register on metal detectors and you dont have to buy ammo or get a gun license","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T17:46:19-08:00","id":1190076,"title":"","content":"Why wouldn't it register on metal detectors, It's a SMG, not a glock. It's made of metal not bone and flesh. And you can't get a license for an Automatic weapon. They aren't legal to own in any industrial country for a civilian. just because mortals don't recognize it when they see it in it's resting state doesn't mean it isn't going to be detected by machines. I had said that the resting state was the equal of carrying the same piece of equipment in a mundane holster concealed by baggy/loose clothing. A metal detector would still pick that up. The illusion of it's mask has lots of metal on it, but also breaks once it wakes up and people see the weapon attached to the hand.<br /> The only advantage you mentioned was not needing to buy ammo, but I am buying ammo other by spending Glamour. A human character just needs to have 1 point of the resources merit to afford bullets and I'm only buying 1 clip for a much rarer resource.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 02-27-2018, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T19:06:05-08:00","id":1190099,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:georgia, serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Tenebrous Prison of the Black Crusader</span></span></b><br /> This suit of Black baroque plate armor was forged by the hands of one of the keepers. This armor is black as midnight in it's mien and etched with golden patterns. While terrifyingly beautiful to behold it is also a hell for the one entombed within it. The armor is attached using flesh hooks and sears into the flesh of the wearer. It cannot be removed without risking the life of the one inside, except for 2 pieces. The pelvic plate and helm, for allowing the wearer to tend to the needs of the flesh. Theses are the only pieces not attached by the searing flesh hooks.<br /> This armor causes the wearer to bear 2 points of aggravated damage at all times while the armor is attached to their body. This damage cannot be downgraded or healed until the armor is removed. Removing a piece other than the helm or pelvic plate causes 3L damage to the wearer. or 2L if done by an expert surgeon at a hospital. The armor has the following pieces. x2 Gauntlet, x2 bracer, x2 vambrace , x2 Paldron, Helm, Breast plate, Greaves (with removable pelvic plate), Shin Plates x2, Boots x2, Soft armor gambison. It's mask is the emotional armor of the biker, in their protective leathers.<br /> <br /> <b>Blessing of the Black Crusade: </b>While wearing the suit the wearer benefits from a +2 bonus to all strength rolls, and is not subject to the normal minimum bashing damage. This armor cannot be combined with any magic that would normally grant an armor bonus.<br /> The armors stats are as below The strength required is before the bonus it grants. <br /> Teneberus Prison of the Black Crusader<br /> <b>Value:</b> 4/4 <b>Strength:</b> 3 <b>Defense</b> -3 <b>Speed</b> -4<br /> <b>Catch:</b> The wearer swears an oath to an enemy at the beginning of the battle that they will kill them, and during the battle kills them, and claimed their head as a trophy.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Removing the armor, provided that didn't kill them, is likely to cause sever withdrawal symptoms in the host. Following the addiction path, until they either willfully return to it or go 1 year without it.<br /> <b>Special:</b> As above the armor causes the host to have a constant 2A damage that cannot be healed or reduced by any means as long as the armor is on. Removal of any of the armor pieces other than the two mentioned above causes sever damage to the body, and removal of the armor is likely to cause death. The armor will reshape it's self for a new host if put on by a new hosts either 1 year after it's removal from the old host, or if the old host dies.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo this is more of a 2 right?<br /> Edit: That said...I just realized in naming these...I've been playing way to much Exalted: Abyssals and named a few to many soul steel artifacts. To be honest in writing this I almost goofed up and said motes instead of glamour.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: As another note, the armor like all his gear is metal. Titanium or some other none iron metal, but still metal and still easily picked up by metal detectors. Kinda question if a catch is needed since it doesn't really have an activated ability and the +2 strength is constant, and being pretty much paid for by the constant 2A damage. The bonus to Armor is being paid for in a worse defense penalty, and mobility penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 02-28-2018, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T05:35:42-08:00","id":1190218,"title":"","content":"It's up to you, but I'd see the armor that cannot be removed as more of a feature of his Mien (ie merits and kith stuff) than a separate token, as I said above. Also, even with the damage, which I now see is a bigger drawback on a player character than I realized before, 6/4 is kinda ridiculous. What could even hurt him above the minimum one bashing damage in that armor? I'd put it more in line with Low Satiety Unbreakable Atavism, which is supposed to be PC-balanced, at 4/3. Perhaps ignoring minimum bashing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 02-28-2018, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T06:21:46-08:00","id":1190239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1189784-help-please-in-putting-my-character-to-paper?p=1190218#post1190218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's up to you, but I'd see the armor that cannot be removed as more of a feature of his Mien (ie merits and kith stuff) than a separate token, as I said above. Also, even with the damage, which I now see is a bigger drawback on a player character than I realized before, 6/4 is kinda ridiculous. What could even hurt him above the minimum one bashing damage in that armor? I'd put it more in line with Satiety Expenditure Unbreakable Atavism, which is supposed to be PC-balanced, at 4/3. Perhaps ignoring minimum bashing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. but I think I'll split the difference with you, if you think this is still balanced and set it to 4/4, and ignores the minimum bashing damage. I'll pull the catch out, since the drawbacks are bad enough. I'll also add a bit about the armor not being compatible with other magics or effects that provide armor.<br /> EDIT: Whoa! Wait a second spend a safety or just low safety Unbreakable? I just read unbreakable. Spend turns all lethal damage into bashing damage, and ignore all incomibing bashing(IE damage that would have started as bashing before unbreakable reduction), and it can by combined with body armor. I'll assume you meant you were changing that last part about negating native bashing damage to preventing the minimum damage.<br /> <br /> Though with the armor value so close to the original armor's should I change back the defense penalty?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 02-28-2018, 09:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T14:14:37-08:00","id":1190432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1189784-help-please-in-putting-my-character-to-paper?p=1190076#post1190076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you can't get a license for an Automatic weapon. They aren't legal to own in any industrial country for a civilian.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, any automatic weapons registered prior to 1986 are legal to own in the United States. This includes ~11 M134 miniguns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","user":"Gallus","date":". 02-28-2018, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T16:31:56-08:00","id":1190481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gallus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1189784-help-please-in-putting-my-character-to-paper?p=1190432#post1190432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, any automatic weapons registered prior to 1986 are legal to own in the United States. This includes ~11 M134 miniguns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. It\u2019s value will need be considered. But good point.<br /> <br /> I guess it could also be licensed for use in a &quot;Private Security&quot; corporate license since I'm security for the court I think the Autumn Monarch might spring for it<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 02-28-2018, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T19:25:24-08:00","id":1190533,"title":"","content":"Okay I...am stumped on this one. I think I need big help.<br /> Here is the thing I am taking inspiration from<br /> Drach'nyen <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Drach'nyen</b> is the name of a powerful <a href=\"http://warhammer40k.wikia.com/wiki/Daemon\" target=\"_blank\">daemon</a> that has been known by many names in the history of Mankind, amongst them the &quot;Echo of the First Murder&quot; and the &quot;End of Empires&quot;. Although its existence is closely linked to the shedding of blood, Drach'nyen has no ties to the <a href=\"http://warhammer40k.wikia.com/wiki/Khorne\" target=\"_blank\">Blood God</a>, being powerful enough to be an independent Chaos entity. The daemon currently resides within a <a href=\"http://warhammer40k.wikia.com/wiki/Daemon_Weapon\" target=\"_blank\">Daemon Sword</a> of the same name wielded by the <a href=\"http://warhammer40k.wikia.com/wiki/Warmaster\" target=\"_blank\">Warmaster</a> of <a href=\"http://warhammer40k.wikia.com/wiki/Chaos\" target=\"_blank\">Chaos</a> <a href=\"http://warhammer40k.wikia.com/wiki/Abaddon_the_Despoiler\" target=\"_blank\">Abaddon the Despoiler</a>, master of the <a href=\"http://warhammer40k.wikia.com/wiki/Black_Legion\" target=\"_blank\">Black Legion</a>, former gene-son of the <a href=\"http://warhammer40k.wikia.com/wiki/Primarch\" target=\"_blank\">Primarch</a> <a href=\"http://warhammer40k.wikia.com/wiki/Horus\" target=\"_blank\">Horus</a>, and most favoured servant of the <a href=\"http://warhammer40k.wikia.com/wiki/Ruinous_Powers\" target=\"_blank\">Ruinous Powers</a>.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The arcane blade borne by Abaddon is so powerful that it can rend reality apart where the weapon strikes. <i>Drach'nyen</i> can rip through armour, flesh and bone without resistance. The <a href=\"http://warhammer40k.wikia.com/wiki/Daemonic\" target=\"_blank\">daemonic</a> spirit animating this fell weapon can alter the blade's appearance, revealing the skulls and faces of the souls it has devoured. Copied from </span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Drach'nyen rules from Source <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> +1 Strength, AP -3 Damage d3<br /> on a roll of a 1 (on a d6) causes 1 wound to the owner. On a 2+ it gets that many extra attacks. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So umm...<br /> +1 to the damage of a basic sword? <br /> Spend 1 glamour to grant AP 2, as the sword becomes sheathed in an sinister energy?<br /> <br /> The problem is action economy so attacks aren't a good option.<br /> <br /> I have to wonder if this might be better suited to a werewolf fetish than a token? Which makes me wonder...how much my keeper sought to invest in creating the realism of the attack she made on the story that was 30 years stagnant. How I picture it is her domain bumped against this toxic swamp/forrest of bubbling, stagnation. A putrid garden of horror where in lies a story that is been held in decay and rotting putretressence for 30 human years. And that filthy concept that a story, or concept should persist like that seeped at the boarders of her domain, threatened to taint her dominion.<br /> <br /> So how faithful to the original would she need to be, in order to make something she could feed into the dreams of the humans who control that story to force them to make it move and thus drain that cesspool, and save her property values...I mean home?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T19:28:22-08:00","id":1190535,"title":"","content":"Weird...I just made a post but it was labeled unapproved? What the?<br /> <br /> Edit: okay it appeared as the post before this one. Must have been the spoilers? Or some kind of keyword trip? Weird. Anyway guess it just needed human review to make sure I wasn\u2019t spreading smut or something.<br /> On word...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 03-01-2018, 02:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T04:50:36-08:00","id":1191307,"title":"","content":"<u><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Drac'nyen</span></span></b></u><br /> This is forged from faerie titan steel, sharpened to a edge that can cut sound, and infused with wrathful spirit. It is a copy of Drach'neyen the demon sword. Daemons of hate and wrath are technically in short supply in Arcadia, and brokering a deal with a werewolf to infuse a spirit into the blade might have had unintended costs. Thus the serfs who produced the visual replicas of the fictions villains equipment captured the Arcadian essence of a dragon, that raw power and aggression were thought to be close enough and this was forced into the blade. Not quite a daemon but close enough for all intents and purposes. The change to the name reflects this change to draconic power. The blade when unsheathed glows with a pale light of vengeance and the raw destructive energy of a dragon. Should the dragon spirit within the blade be fed a small amount of glamour than the pale light becomes a blinding force as the hungry dragon goes to work. Seeking to sup upon the life of all it slaughters.<br /> <br /> <b>Violence Unleashed:</b> The dragon's appetite now wet seeks to gorge it's self empowering the blade to do more so that it can feast upon the life of slain. By spending a glamour this weapon gains +2 piercing and 9 again.<br /> <b>Catch:</b> You swear an oath to the blade to kill a specific person, and then do so that turn or the next no later. The catch goes into effect then.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> If the wielder should happen to miss with an attack against a foe with a lower supernatural tolerance than their own, Drac'nyen's pride will cause it to wound it's user. This causes a damage roll equivalent to the damage of the weapon, that cannot be modified by armor. Oh...and the sword talks telepathically to it's owner, it's a personality is exactly what one would expect from the essence of dragon hood, it's a pompous, arrogant, self aggrandizing, prick. Sadly the owner cannot respond back telepathically. This can cause a -1 to social rolls if anyone not aware (and believing), sees you talking to your sword...<br /> <br /> <i>Drac'nyen</i><br /> Damage 4, init -3, Strength 2 Size 3, Piercing 2<br /> <br /> Everything here look balanced? Also what level are we at for Token merit. I'm aiming for 3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}